From d21e17a0ff524ec379c0bd09cce101189b42329e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:45:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] Round 4: Reuse saturation properties as the near
 inverse bracket value

The bracket end at the saturation temperature repeats the saturation
state's own computation, so its enthalpy or entropy is taken from the
pair and only the far end (273.16 K or 1073.15 K) is evaluated. The
inverse now derives its pressure from the pair, and a unit test asserts
the bit equality across the pressure range. Results are bit-identical.

Workload: domain (48 candidates at 950 K), matrix API both sides.
Official 11-sample run: 0.556 ms -> 0.491 ms, 1.13x (paired 1.14x).
41-sample confirmation: 0.558 ms -> 0.495 ms, paired 1.13x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
